# ROWNAA — Phase 0: Design System & CSS Architecture

> This is the FOUNDATION of the entire UI. Every developer building any phase must read this first. No component should use hardcoded colors, sizes, or fonts that are not defined here.

---

## 1. Brand Identity & Tone

- **Platform Name:** Rownaa
- **Tagline:** "Book a car, anywhere you're headed."
- **Tone:** Premium, trustworthy, professional. NOT playful, NOT generic, NOT AI-default.
- **Inspiration:** The premium feel of Uber/Pathao but adapted for scheduled rentals in Bangladesh.
- **Target Users:** Urban professionals booking cars via mobile phone. They expect an app-like experience.

---

## 2. Color System (Exact Values — No Deviation)

### Primary Palette
| Token Name | HEX | HSL | Usage |
|---|---|---|---|
| `--color-brand-primary` | `#0A1628` | `hsl(218, 58%, 10%)` | Main background, navbars, headers |
| `--color-brand-secondary` | `#112240` | `hsl(214, 60%, 16%)` | Card backgrounds, sidebar |
| `--color-brand-accent` | `#F4A622` | `hsl(38, 91%, 55%)` | CTAs, active states, highlights (Rownaa Gold) |
| `--color-brand-accent-hover` | `#D4891A` | `hsl(35, 80%, 47%)` | Hover state on accent buttons |
| `--color-surface` | `#172A45` | `hsl(214, 55%, 18%)` | Section panels, card surfaces |
| `--color-surface-elevated` | `#1E3A5F` | `hsl(211, 52%, 24%)` | Elevated cards, dropdowns |

### Text Colors
| Token Name | HEX | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| `--color-text-primary` | `#F0F4F8` | Main body text on dark backgrounds |
| `--color-text-secondary` | `#8FA3BE` | Captions, labels, secondary info |
| `--color-text-muted` | `#4A6280` | Placeholder text, disabled states |
| `--color-text-on-accent` | `#0A1628` | Text ON the gold accent button |

### Status Colors
| Token Name | HEX | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| `--color-status-pending` | `#F59E0B` | Pending booking badge |
| `--color-status-confirmed` | `#3B82F6` | Confirmed booking badge |
| `--color-status-ongoing` | `#8B5CF6` | Ongoing trip badge |
| `--color-status-completed` | `#10B981` | Completed badge |
| `--color-status-cancelled` | `#EF4444` | Cancelled badge |
| `--color-status-rejected` | `#DC2626` | Rejected document badge |

### Gradients (Use these exact definitions)
```css
--gradient-hero: linear-gradient(135deg, #0A1628 0%, #1E3A5F 60%, #112240 100%);
--gradient-card: linear-gradient(160deg, #172A45 0%, #112240 100%);
--gradient-accent: linear-gradient(90deg, #F4A622 0%, #D4891A 100%);
--gradient-glass: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.08) 0%, rgba(255,255,255,0.02) 100%);
```

---

## 3. Typography System

### Font Import (Add to `<head>` on every HTML page)
```html
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800&family=Outfit:wght@400;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
```

### Font Roles
| Token | Font | Weight | Usage |
|---|---|---|---|
| `--font-display` | `'Outfit', sans-serif` | 700–800 | Hero titles, page headings |
| `--font-body` | `'Inter', sans-serif` | 400–600 | All body text, forms, buttons |

### Type Scale (Desktop)
| Token | Size | Line Height | Usage |
|---|---|---|---|
| `--text-hero` | `clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem)` | 1.1 | Hero section H1 |
| `--text-h1` | `2.25rem (36px)` | 1.2 | Page titles |
| `--text-h2` | `1.75rem (28px)` | 1.3 | Section headings |
| `--text-h3` | `1.25rem (20px)` | 1.4 | Card headings |
| `--text-body` | `1rem (16px)` | 1.6 | Body copy |
| `--text-small` | `0.875rem (14px)` | 1.5 | Labels, captions |
| `--text-xs` | `0.75rem (12px)` | 1.4 | Badges, timestamps |

### Type Scale (Mobile — defined in `mobile.css`)
| Token | Size | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| `--text-hero` | `2rem (32px)` | Hero H1 on mobile |
| `--text-h1` | `1.5rem (24px)` | Page titles on mobile |
| `--text-h2` | `1.25rem (20px)` | Section headings on mobile |
| `--text-h3` | `1.1rem (17.6px)` | Card headings on mobile |
| `--text-body` | `0.9375rem (15px)` | Body copy on mobile |
| `--text-small` | `0.8125rem (13px)` | Labels on mobile |

---

## 4. Spacing System

```css
--space-xs:   4px;
--space-sm:   8px;
--space-md:  16px;
--space-lg:  24px;
--space-xl:  32px;
--space-2xl: 48px;
--space-3xl: 64px;
--space-4xl: 96px;
```

---

## 5. Border Radius & Shadow System

```css
--radius-sm:   6px;   /* small tags, badges */
--radius-md:  12px;   /* input fields, small cards */
--radius-lg:  16px;   /* main cards */
--radius-xl:  24px;   /* feature cards, modals */
--radius-full: 9999px; /* pills, toggle buttons */

--shadow-card: 0 4px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
--shadow-elevated: 0 8px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
--shadow-accent: 0 4px 20px rgba(244, 166, 34, 0.3);
--shadow-inset: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.07);
```

---

## 6. Component Specifications

### 6A. Buttons

#### Primary Button (Accent CTA)
- Background: `var(--gradient-accent)`
- Text Color: `var(--color-text-on-accent)` (`#0A1628`)
- Font: `Inter`, 600 weight, `15px`
- Padding: `14px 28px` (Desktop) | `12px 24px` (Mobile)
- Border Radius: `var(--radius-full)` (pill shape)
- Border: none
- Shadow: `var(--shadow-accent)`
- Hover: scale(1.03), brighter shadow — transition 0.2s ease
- Active: scale(0.98)
- Disabled: opacity 0.5, cursor not-allowed, no scale

#### Secondary Button (Ghost/Outline)
- Background: transparent
- Border: `1.5px solid rgba(244, 166, 34, 0.5)`
- Text: `var(--color-brand-accent)`
- All other properties same as Primary except shadow = none
- Hover: Background fills with `rgba(244, 166, 34, 0.1)`

#### Danger Button (Reject/Cancel)
- Background: `rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.15)`
- Border: `1.5px solid rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.4)`
- Text: `#EF4444`
- Hover: Background `rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.25)`

#### Icon Button (Action icons in tables/cards)
- Size: `36px × 36px` (Desktop) | `44px × 44px` (Mobile — touch target)
- Background: `var(--color-surface-elevated)`
- Border Radius: `var(--radius-md)`
- Hover: background lightens

### 6B. Input Fields & Forms

- Background: `rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05)`
- Border: `1.5px solid rgba(143, 163, 190, 0.2)`
- Border Radius: `var(--radius-md)` (12px)
- Text Color: `var(--color-text-primary)`
- Placeholder: `var(--color-text-muted)`
- Font Size: `15px` body, `14px` label above field
- Label: Uppercase, letter-spacing 0.05em, `var(--color-text-secondary)`, 12px
- Padding: `14px 16px`
- Focus State: Border color → `var(--color-brand-accent)`, box-shadow → `0 0 0 3px rgba(244,166,34,0.2)`
- Error State: Border color → `#EF4444`, error message text below in red `12px`
- **Mobile:** height minimum `50px`, font-size `16px` (prevents iOS zoom)

#### Select Dropdowns
- Same styling as input fields
- Custom arrow icon using `appearance: none` + SVG background-image
- Options styled with dark background matching `--color-surface-elevated`

#### File Upload Areas
- Dashed border: `2px dashed rgba(143, 163, 190, 0.3)`
- Background: `rgba(255,255,255,0.03)`
- Drag area: Shows cloud-upload icon + "Click to upload or drag & drop"
- After upload: Shows file thumbnail (image preview or PDF icon) with file name and a remove ×

### 6C. Cards

#### Standard Listing Card (Car listing, booking summary)
- Background: `var(--gradient-card)`
- Border: `1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07)`
- Border Radius: `var(--radius-lg)` (16px)
- Shadow: `var(--shadow-card)`
- Padding: `20px` (Desktop) | `16px` (Mobile)
- Hover: transform translateY(-4px), shadow intensifies — transition 0.25s ease

#### Status Badge
- Border Radius: `var(--radius-full)`
- Padding: `4px 10px`
- Font: `Inter` 600, `12px`
- Colors: Use status tokens defined in Section 2

#### Glassmorphism Card (for hero overlays, stats panels)
- Background: `var(--gradient-glass)`
- Backdrop-filter: `blur(16px)`
- Border: `1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1)`
- Border Radius: `var(--radius-xl)`

---

## 7. Animation Rules

- **Duration Standard:** 200ms for micro (hover), 350ms for transitions (page loads, modals), 500ms for entrance animations
- **Easing:** Always `cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1)` for smooth feel
- **Entrance Animation:** `fadeInUp` — elements enter from `translateY(20px)` opacity 0 → translateY(0) opacity 1
- **Stagger:** Each list item enters with a 60ms delay after the previous
- **No infinite loops** unless it is a loading spinner
- **Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`** — wrap animations in the media query

---

## 8. CSS File Architecture (CRITICAL — NEVER MERGE THESE)

```
/styles/
├── global.css         ← CSS variables, fonts, resets, utility classes ONLY
├── desktop.css        ← All layout, grid, hover effects for screen > 768px
├── mobile.css         ← Complete standalone app-like styles for screen <= 768px
├── admin.css          ← Admin panel specific desktop styles
├── admin-mobile.css   ← Admin panel app-like mobile styles
└── animations.css     ← All @keyframes, transition classes
```

### How Stylesheets Are Linked (in every HTML `<head>`)
```html
<!-- Always loaded -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/global.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/animations.css">

<!-- Desktop only -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/desktop.css" media="screen and (min-width: 769px)">

<!-- Mobile only -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/mobile.css" media="screen and (max-width: 768px)">
```

### For Admin Pages
```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/global.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/animations.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/admin.css" media="screen and (min-width: 769px)">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/admin-mobile.css" media="screen and (max-width: 768px)">
```

> **STRICT RULE:** `desktop.css` must NEVER contain any `max-width` media queries. `mobile.css` must NEVER contain any `min-width` media queries. They are completely independent stylesheets serving completely different layouts.

---

## 9. Icon System

- **Library:** Lucide Icons (lightweight, consistent) — loaded via CDN or npm
- **Size Standard:** 20px (inline), 24px (nav), 32px (feature icons), 48px (hero icons)
- **Color:** Always inherit from parent or use `var(--color-text-secondary)` as default
- **Active State:** Icon color → `var(--color-brand-accent)`

---

## 10. Responsive Breakpoints

```css
/* Defined in global.css for reference */
/* Mobile:  max-width: 768px  → handled by mobile.css */
/* Desktop: min-width: 769px  → handled by desktop.css */
/* Wide:    min-width: 1280px → overrides within desktop.css */
```
